{"step_index":1767,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T06:15:10Z","input_tokens":2857,"cache_read_tokens":191999,"output_tokens":9143,"thinking":"Avoiding potential PowerShell quoting complexities, a JavaScript script will be created to generate the problem data. This script will reside in a temporary directory, ensuring a clean and manageable approach to file creation. The generated JavaScript file will adhere to a defined structure for each problem object, confirmed by inspecting a sample object.\n\n\nThe provided data represents a single LeetCode problem, \"Two Sum\".  The focus is now on constructing a JavaScript script to generate a structured dataset of 300 similar problems. Each problem's attributes include ID, LeetCode number, title, difficulty, topic, pattern, description, time and space complexity, starter code, and example inputs/outputs. This script will ensure data integrity by validating the uniqueness of IDs, titles, and LeetCode numbers. The generated dataset will be written to `app_build/dsa_problems.js`.\n\n\nThe initial step is to define the problem distribution across the identified algorithmic topics. A structured allocation of 300 problems across 18 topics is being created to establish a comprehensive data set. This will be the foundation for generating the problem data.\n\nA script will be developed to generate the data set in `app_build/dsa_problems.js`.  This script will enforce data integrity through validation checks, including uniqueness of IDs and titles, valid difficulty levels, and ensuring all required fields are populated. The Python starter code will also be checked for syntax validity.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"// scratch/generate_dataset.js\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\n\nconst problems = [\n  // ==========================================\n  // TOPIC 1: ARRAYS & HASHING (30 Problems)\n  // ==========================================\n  {\n    id: 1,\n    leetcodeNumber: 1,\n    title: \"Two Sum\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Hash Map Lookup\",\n    description: \"Find indices of two numbers that add up to a target using a dictionary for instant lookups.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    starterCode: `def twoSum(nums, target):\n    prevMap = {}\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        diff = target - nums[i]\n        if diff in prevMap:\n            return [prevMap[diff], i]\n        prevMap[nums[i]] = i\n    return []\n\nnums = [2, 7, 11, 15]\ntarget = 9\nans = twoSum(nums, target)\nprint(\"Indices:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 2,\n    leetcodeNumber: 217,\n    title: \"Contains Duplicate\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Hash Set\",\n    description: \"Determine if any value appears at least twice in the array using a set.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    starterCode: `def containsDuplicate(nums):\n    seen = set()\n    for n in nums:\n        if n in seen:\n            return True\n        seen.add(n)\n    return False\n\nnums = [1, 2, 3, 1]\nans = containsDuplicate(nums)\nprint(\"Has duplicate:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 3,\n    leetcodeNumber: 242,\n    title: \"Valid Anagram\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Frequency Counter\",\n    description: \"Check if string t is an anagram of string s by counting character occurrences.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def isAnagram(s, t):\n    if len(s) != len(t):\n        return False\n    countS = {}\n    countT = {}\n    for ch in s:\n        countS[ch] = countS.get(ch, 0) + 1\n    for ch in t:\n        countT[ch] = countT.get(ch, 0) + 1\n    return countS == countT\n\ns = \"anagram\"\nt = \"nagaram\"\nans = isAnagram(s, t)\nprint(\"Is anagram:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 4,\n    leetcodeNumber: 49,\n    title: \"Group Anagrams\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Categorization by Key\",\n    description: \"Group strings that are anagrams together by sorting or frequency tuple keys.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(m * n log n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(m * n)\",\n    starterCode: `def groupAnagrams(strs):\n    ansMap = {}\n    for s in strs:\n        key = \"\".join(sorted(s))\n        if key not in ansMap:\n            ansMap[key] = []\n        ansMap[key].append(s)\n    return list(ansMap.values())\n\nstrs = [\"eat\", \"tea\", \"tan\", \"ate\", \"nat\", \"bat\"]\ngroups = groupAnagrams(strs)\nprint(\"Groups:\", groups)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 5,\n    leetcodeNumber: 347,\n    title: \"Top K Frequent Elements\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Bucket Sort / Frequency Map\",\n    description: \"Find the k most frequent elements in an array using frequency counting.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    starterCode: `def topKFrequent(nums, k):\n    count = {}\n    for n in nums:\n        count[n] = count.get(n, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Sort keys by frequency descending\n    sorted_items = sorted(count.items(), key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n    return [item[0] for item in sorted_items[:k]]\n\nnums = [1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3]\nk = 2\nans = topKFrequent(nums, k)\nprint(\"Top K:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 6,\n    leetcodeNumber: 238,\n    title: \"Product of Array Except Self\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Prefix & Suffix Products\",\n    description: \"Calculate products of all elements except nums[i] in O(n) without division.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def productExceptSelf(nums):\n    res = [1] * len(nums)\n    prefix = 1\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        res[i] = prefix\n        prefix *= nums[i]\n    postfix = 1\n    for i in range(len(nums) - 1, -1, -1):\n        res[i] *= postfix\n        postfix *= nums[i]\n    return res\n\nnums = [1, 2, 3, 4]\nans = productExceptSelf(nums)\nprint(\"Products:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 7,\n    leetcodeNumber: 36,\n    title: \"Valid Sudoku\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"2D Hash Set Tracking\",\n    description: \"Verify that each row, column, and 3x3 box contains unique digits 1-9.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def isValidSudoku(board):\n    rows = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    cols = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    boxes = [set() for _ in range(9)]\n    \n    for r in range(9):\n        for c in range(9):\n            val = board[r][c]\n            if val == \".\":\n                continue\n            box_idx = (r // 3) * 3 + (c // 3)\n            if val in rows[r] or val in cols[c] or val in boxes[box_idx]:\n                return False\n            rows[r].add(val)\n            cols[c].add(val)\n            boxes[box_idx].add(val)\n    return True\n\n# Simple partial 4x4-style mini board for tracing\nboard = [\n  [\"5\",\"3\",\".\",\".\",\"7\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\"],\n  [\"6\",\".\",\".\",\"1\",\"9\",\"5\",\".\",\".\",\".\"],\n  [\".\",\"9\",\"8\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"6\",\".\"],\n  [\"8\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"6\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"3\"],\n  [\"4\",\".\",\".\",\"8\",\".\",\"3\",\".\",\".\",\"1\"],\n  [\"7\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"2\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"6\"],\n  [\".\",\"6\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"2\",\"8\",\".\"],\n  [\".\",\".\",\".\",\"4\",\"1\",\"9\",\".\",\".\",\"5\"],\n  [\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"8\",\".\",\".\",\"7\",\"9\"]\n]\nprint(\"Is valid:\", isValidSudoku(board))`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 8,\n    leetcodeNumber: 128,\n    title: \"Longest Consecutive Sequence\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Hash Set Streak Building\",\n    description: \"Find length of the longest consecutive elements sequence in O(n) time.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    starterCode: `def longestConsecutive(nums):\n    numSet = set(nums)\n    longest = 0\n    for n in numSet:\n        # Check if n is the start of a sequence\n        if (n - 1) not in numSet:\n            length = 1\n            while (n + length) in numSet:\n                length += 1\n            if length > longest:\n                longest = length\n    return longest\n\nnums = [100, 4, 200, 1, 3, 2]\nans = longestConsecutive(nums)\nprint(\"Longest streak:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 9,\n    leetcodeNumber: 169,\n    title: \"Majority Element\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Boyer-Moore Voting\",\n    description: \"Find the element appearing more than n/2 times in O(1) space.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def majorityElement(nums):\n    candidate = None\n    count = 0\n    for n in nums:\n        if count == 0:\n            candidate = n\n        if n == candidate:\n            count += 1\n        else:\n            count -= 1\n    return candidate\n\nnums = [2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2]\nans = majorityElement(nums)\nprint(\"Majority element:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 10,\n    leetcodeNumber: 136,\n    title: \"Single Number\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Bitwise XOR / Hash Set\",\n    description: \"Every element appears twice except for one. Find that single element.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def singleNumber(nums):\n    res = 0\n    for n in nums:\n        res ^= n\n    return res\n\nnums = [4, 1, 2, 1, 2]\nans = singleNumber(nums)\nprint(\"Single number:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 11,\n    leetcodeNumber: 448,\n    title: \"Find All Numbers Disappeared in an Array\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"In-Place Index Tagging\",\n    description: \"Find all integers in range [1, n] that do not appear in the array.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def findDisappearedNumbers(nums):\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        idx = abs(nums[i]) - 1\n        if nums[idx] > 0:\n            nums[idx] = -nums[idx]\n    \n    missing = []\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        if nums[i] > 0:\n            missing.append(i + 1)\n    return missing\n\nnums = [4, 3, 2, 7, 8, 2, 3, 1]\nans = findDisappearedNumbers(nums)\nprint(\"Missing numbers:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 12,\n    leetcodeNumber: 268,\n    title: \"Missing Number\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Arithmetic Sum Formula\",\n    description: \"Given array containing n distinct numbers in range [0, n], return missing number.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def missingNumber(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    expected_sum = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    actual_sum = sum(nums)\n    return expected_sum - actual_sum\n\nnums = [3, 0, 1]\nans = missingNumber(nums)\nprint(\"Missing:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 13,\n    leetcodeNumber: 283,\n    title: \"Move Zeroes\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Two Pointers Writer\",\n    description: \"Move all 0s to end while maintaining relative order of non-zero elements.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def moveZeroes(nums):\n    writer = 0\n    for reader in range(len(nums)):\n        if nums[reader] != 0:\n            nums[writer], nums[reader] = nums[reader], nums[writer]\n            writer += 1\n    return nums\n\nnums = [0, 1, 0, 3, 12]\nmoveZeroes(nums)\nprint(\"Moved zeroes:\", nums)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 14,\n    leetcodeNumber: 66,\n    title: \"Plus One\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Array Digit Simulation\",\n    description: \"Increment large integer represented as array of digits by one.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def plusOne(digits):\n    for i in range(len(digits) - 1, -1, -1):\n        if digits[i] < 9:\n            digits[i] += 1\n            return digits\n        digits[i] = 0\n    return [1] + digits\n\ndigits = [1, 2, 9]\nans = plusOne(digits)\nprint(\"Plus one:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 15,\n    leetcodeNumber: 485,\n    title: \"Max Consecutive Ones\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Linear Streak Counter\",\n    description: \"Find the maximum number of consecutive 1s in a binary array.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def findMaxConsecutiveOnes(nums):\n    max_count = 0\n    curr = 0\n    for n in nums:\n        if n == 1:\n            curr += 1\n            if curr > max_count:\n                max_count = curr\n        else:\n            curr = 0\n    return max_count\n\nnums = [1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1]\nans = findMaxConsecutiveOnes(nums)\nprint(\"Max consecutive ones:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 16,\n    leetcodeNumber: 560,\n    title: \"Subarray Sum Equals K\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Prefix Sum + Hash Map\",\n    description: \"Find total number of subarrays whose sum equals k using prefix frequencies.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    starterCode: `def subarraySum(nums, k):\n    count = 0\n    curr_sum = 0\n    prefix_map = {0: 1}\n    for n in nums:\n        curr_sum += n\n        diff = curr_sum - k\n        if diff in prefix_map:\n            count += prefix_map[diff]\n        prefix_map[curr_sum] = prefix_map.get(curr_sum, 0) + 1\n    return count\n\nnums = [1, 1, 1]\nk = 2\nans = subarraySum(nums, k)\nprint(\"Count of subarrays:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 17,\n    leetcodeNumber: 525,\n    title: \"Contiguous Array\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Prefix Balance Tracking\",\n    description: \"Find maximum length of contiguous subarray with equal number of 0s and 1s.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    starterCode: `def findMaxLength(nums):\n    max_len = 0\n    balance = 0\n    seen = {0: -1}\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        balance += 1 if nums[i] == 1 else -1\n        if balance in seen:\n            length = i - seen[balance]\n            if length > max_len:\n                max_len = length\n        else:\n            seen[balance] = i\n    return max_len\n\nnums = [0, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0]\nans = findMaxLength(nums)\nprint(\"Max length:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 18,\n    leetcodeNumber: 189,\n    title: \"Rotate Array\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Array Reversal Triplets\",\n    description: \"Rotate array to right by k steps using in-place triple reversal.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def rotate(nums, k):\n    k = k % len(nums)\n    def reverse(start, end):\n        while start < end:\n            nums[start], nums[end] = nums[end], nums[start]\n            start += 1\n            end -= 1\n    # 1. Reverse entire array\n    reverse(0, len(nums) - 1)\n    # 2. Reverse first k elements\n    reverse(0, k - 1)\n    # 3. Reverse remaining elements\n    reverse(k, len(nums) - 1)\n    return nums\n\nnums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]\nrotate(nums, 3)\nprint(\"Rotated:\", nums)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 19,\n    leetcodeNumber: 48,\n    title: \"Rotate Image\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Transpose and Reverse\",\n    description: \"Rotate n x n 2D matrix by 90 degrees clockwise in-place.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n^2)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def rotateImage(matrix):\n    n = len(matrix)\n    # Step 1: Transpose matrix\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            matrix[i][j], matrix[j][i] = matrix[j][i], matrix[i][j]\n    # Step 2: Reverse each row\n    for i in range(n):\n        matrix[i].reverse()\n    return matrix\n\nmatrix = [\n    [1, 2, 3],\n    [4, 5, 6],\n    [7, 8, 9]\n]\nrotateImage(matrix)\nprint(\"Rotated matrix:\", matrix)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 20,\n    leetcodeNumber: 73,\n    title: \"Set Matrix Zeroes\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"First Row/Col Markers\",\n    description: \"If an element is 0, set its entire row and column to 0 in-place.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(m * n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def setZeroes(matrix):\n    m = len(matrix)\n    n = len(matrix[0])\n    first_col_zero = False\n    \n    for r in range(m):\n        if matrix[r][0] == 0:\n            first_col_zero = True\n        for c in range(1, n):\n            if matrix[r][c] == 0:\n                matrix[r][0] = 0\n                matrix[0][c] = 0\n                \n    for r in range(1, m):\n        for c in range(1, n):\n            if matrix[r][0] == 0 or matrix[0][c] == 0:\n                matrix[r][c] = 0\n                \n    if matrix[0][0] == 0:\n        for c in range(n):\n            matrix[0][c] = 0\n    if first_col_zero:\n        for r in range(m):\n            matrix[r][0] = 0\n    return matrix\n\nmat = [[1, 1, 1], [1, 0, 1], [1, 1, 1]]\nsetZeroes(mat)\nprint(\"Matrix after zeroes:\", mat)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 21,\n    leetcodeNumber: 54,\n    title: \"Spiral Matrix\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Boundary Shrinking\",\n    description: \"Return all elements of matrix in spiral order by contracting boundaries.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(m * n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def spiralOrder(matrix):\n    res = []\n    top, bottom = 0, len(matrix) - 1\n    left, right = 0, len(matrix[0]) - 1\n    \n    while left <= right and top <= bottom:\n        for c in range(left, right + 1):\n            res.append(matrix[top][c])\n        top += 1\n        for r in range(top, bottom + 1):\n            res.append(matrix[r][right])\n        right -= 1\n        if top <= bottom:\n            for c in range(right, left - 1, -1):\n                res.append(matrix[bottom][c])\n            bottom -= 1\n        if left <= right:\n            for r in range(bottom, top - 1, -1):\n                res.append(matrix[r][left])\n            left += 1\n    return res\n\nmatrix = [\n    [1, 2, 3],\n    [4, 5, 6],\n    [7, 8, 9]\n]\nans = spiralOrder(matrix)\nprint(\"Spiral order:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 22,\n    leetcodeNumber: 75,\n    title: \"Sort Colors\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Dutch National Flag (3 Pointers)\",\n    description: \"Sort array of 0s, 1s, and 2s in-place in a single pass.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def sortColors(nums):\n    low = 0\n    mid = 0\n    high = len(nums) - 1\n    while mid <= high:\n        if nums[mid] == 0:\n            nums[low], nums[mid] = nums[mid], nums[low]\n            low += 1\n            mid += 1\n        elif nums[mid] == 1:\n            mid += 1\n        else:\n            nums[mid], nums[high] = nums[high], nums[mid]\n            high -= 1\n    return nums\n\nnums = [2, 0, 2, 1, 1, 0]\nsortColors(nums)\nprint(\"Sorted colors:\", nums)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 23,\n    leetcodeNumber: 229,\n    title: \"Majority Element II\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Extended Boyer-Moore\",\n    description: \"Find all elements that appear more than n/3 times in linear time and O(1) space.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def majorityElementII(nums):\n    cand1, cand2 = None, None\n    count1, count2 = 0, 0\n    for n in nums:\n        if n == cand1:\n            count1 += 1\n        elif n == cand2:\n            count2 += 1\n        elif count1 == 0:\n            cand1, count1 = n, 1\n        elif count2 == 0:\n            cand2, count2 = n, 1\n        else:\n            count1 -= 1\n            count2 -= 1\n    result = []\n    threshold = len(nums) // 3\n    if nums.count(cand1) > threshold:\n        result.append(cand1)\n    if cand2 != cand1 and nums.count(cand2) > threshold:\n        result.append(cand2)\n    return result\n\nnums = [3, 2, 3]\nans = majorityElementII(nums)\nprint(\"Elements > n/3:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 24,\n    leetcodeNumber: 41,\n    title: \"First Missing Positive\",\n    difficulty: \"Hard\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Index as Hash Key\",\n    description: \"Find the smallest positive integer missing from an unsorted array in O(n) and O(1) space.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def firstMissingPositive(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    for i in range(n):\n        while 1 <= nums[i] <= n and nums[nums[i] - 1] != nums[i]:\n            target_idx = nums[i] - 1\n            nums[i], nums[target_idx] = nums[target_idx], nums[i]\n            \n    for i in range(n):\n        if nums[i] != i + 1:\n            return i + 1\n    return n + 1\n\nnums = [3, 4, -1, 1]\nans = firstMissingPositive(nums)\nprint(\"First missing positive:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 25,\n    leetcodeNumber: 14,\n    title: \"Longest Common Prefix\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Horizontal / Vertical Scanning\",\n    description: \"Find the longest common prefix string amongst an array of strings.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(S)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def longestCommonPrefix(strs):\n    if not strs:\n        return \"\"\n    prefix = strs[0]\n    for s in strs[1:]:\n        while not s.startswith(prefix):\n            prefix = prefix[:-1]\n            if not prefix:\n                return \"\"\n    return prefix\n\nstrs = [\"flower\", \"flow\", \"flight\"]\nans = longestCommonPrefix(strs)\nprint(\"Prefix:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 26,\n    leetcodeNumber: 58,\n    title: \"Length of Last Word\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Right-to-Left Traversal\",\n    description: \"Return length of the last word in a string consisting of non-space characters.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def lengthOfLastWord(s):\n    i = len(s) - 1\n    length = 0\n    while i >= 0 and s[i] == \" \":\n        i -= 1\n    while i >= 0 and s[i] != \" \":\n        length += 1\n        i -= 1\n    return length\n\ns = \"Hello World\"\nans = lengthOfLastWord(s)\nprint(\"Length of last word:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 27,\n    leetcodeNumber: 387,\n    title: \"First Unique Character in a String\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Frequency Counting\",\n    description: \"Find the first non-repeating character in a string and return its index.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def firstUniqChar(s):\n    count = {}\n    for ch in s:\n        count[ch] = count.get(ch, 0) + 1\n    for i, ch in enumerate(s):\n        if count[ch] == 1:\n            return i\n    return -1\n\ns = \"leetcode\"\nans = firstUniqChar(s)\nprint(\"First unique index:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 28,\n    leetcodeNumber: 205,\n    title: \"Isomorphic Strings\",\n    difficulty: \"Easy\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Dual Character Mapping\",\n    description: \"Determine if characters in s can be replaced to get t using bijection maps.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    starterCode: `def isIsomorphic(s, t):\n    if len(s) != len(t):\n        return False\n    mapST, mapTS = {}, {}\n    for c1, c2 in zip(s, t):\n        if (c1 in mapST and mapST[c1] != c2) or (c2 in mapTS and mapTS[c2] != c1):\n            return False\n        mapST[c1] = c2\n        mapTS[c2] = c1\n    return True\n\ns = \"egg\"\nt = \"add\"\nans = isIsomorphic(s, t)\nprint(\"Isomorphic:\", ans)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 29,\n    leetcodeNumber: 271,\n    title: \"Encode and Decode Strings\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Length-Prefix Delimiter\",\n    description: \"Design an algorithm to encode a list of strings to a string and decode back.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    starterCode: `def encode(strs):\n    res = \"\"\n    for s in strs:\n        res += str(len(s)) + \"#\" + s\n    return res\n\ndef decode(s):\n    res, i = [], 0\n    while i < len(s):\n        j = i\n        while s[j] != \"#\":\n            j += 1\n        length = int(s[i:j])\n        res.append(s[j + 1 : j + 1 + length])\n        i = j + 1 + length\n    return res\n\noriginal = [\"neet\", \"code\", \"love\", \"you\"]\nencoded = encode(original)\ndecoded = decode(encoded)\nprint(\"Encoded:\", encoded)\nprint(\"Decoded:\", decoded)`\n  },\n  {\n    id: 30,\n    leetcodeNumber: 380,\n    title: \"Insert Delete GetRandom O(1)\",\n    difficulty: \"Medium\",\n    topic: \"Arrays & Hashing\",\n    pattern: \"Array + Hash Map Swap\",\n    description: \"Design a data structure that supports insert, remove, and getRandom in O(1) time.\",\n    timeComplexity: \"O(1)\",\n    spaceComplexity: \"O(n)\",\n    starterCode: `class RandomizedSet:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.numMap = {}\n        self.numList = []\n        \n    def insert(self, val):\n        if val in self.numMap:\n            return False\n        self.numMap[val] = len(self.numList)\n        self.numList.append(val)\n        return True\n        \n    def remove(self, val):\n        if val not in self.numMap:\n            return False\n        idx = self.numMap[val]\n        last_val = self.numList[-1]\n        self.numList[idx] = last_val\n        self.numMap[last_val] = idx\n        self.numList.pop()\n        del self.numMap[val]\n        return True\n\nr = RandomizedSet()\nprint(\"Insert 10:\", r.insert(10))\nprint(\"Insert 20:\", r.insert(20))\nprint(\"Remove 10:\", r.remove(10))`\n  }\n];\n\nconsole.log(`Generated ${problems.length} array problems`);\n","Description":"Build initial batch of Array problems in scratch/generate_dataset.js","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/generate_dataset.js","toolAction":"Writing scratch generator script","toolSummary":"Create scratch generator script"}}]}
